<p class=3DMsoNormal><b>And there's a clever way to make this a strong fina=
l-year
project<o:p></o:p></b></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Don't present the project as:</p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><b>&quot;I made a quiz app that locks phones.&quot;</b=
></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Present it as:</p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><b>&quot;A supervised mobile assessment platform that
combines controlled examination sessions, application-level security
mechanisms, automated assessment, and real-time performance analytics.&quot=
;</b></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Then your research/technical contribution becomes:</p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><b>Assessment<o:p></o:p></b></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>How can quizzes be conducted efficiently?</p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><b>Security<o:p></o:p></b></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>How can opportunities for digital cheating be reduced =
on
students' smartphones?</p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><b>Reliability<o:p></o:p></b></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>How can students continue an assessment despite tempor=
ary
connectivity problems?</p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><b>Analytics<o:p></o:p></b></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>How can quiz results provide useful information about
student learning?</p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>That's a <b>substantially stronger project</b> than si=
mply
implementing a lockdown API.</p>

