<p class=3DMsoNormal><b>My recommendation<o:p></o:p></b></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><b>Yes, include lockdown mode =97 but make it an optio=
nal
Android-specific feature.</b></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Your minimum viable project should work without it:</p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Teacher creates &#8594; Students join &#8594; Teacher =
starts
&#8594; Students take quiz &#8594; Automatic grading &#8594; Analytics.</p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Then:</p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><b>Advanced feature:</b> Secure Exam Mode <span
style=3D'font-family:"Segoe UI Emoji",sans-serif;mso-bidi-font-family:"Sego=
e UI Emoji"'>&#128274;</span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>If the lockdown implementation proves difficult, you h=
aven't
lost your entire project.</p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>And if you successfully implement it, it becomes one o=
f the
features that differentiates your project from a normal Google Forms/Kahoot=
-style
quiz system.</p>

